@page "/features"
@layout MarketingLayout

<PageTitle>Features — Brainy</PageTitle>
<HeadContent>
    <meta name="description" content="Everything a second brain needs: frictionless capture, PARA organization, progressive summarization, tasks and Today, goals, outputs, and trustworthy AI assistance." />
</HeadContent>

<section class="mkt-hero">
    <div class="mkt-wrap">
        <span class="mkt-eyebrow mkt-rise">The full index</span>
        <h1 class="mkt-title mkt-rise mkt-d1" style="max-width: 14em; font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5vw, 3.8rem);">
            Everything a second brain needs. <em>Nothing it doesn't.</em>
        </h1>
        <p class="mkt-lead mkt-rise mkt-d2" style="margin-top: 1.4rem;">
            Every feature exists to save you time, reduce mental clutter, and turn
            what you know into something useful. No storage for storage's sake.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="mkt-section">
    <div class="mkt-wrap">
        <div class="mkt-feature-list mkt-rise mkt-d3">
            <article class="mkt-feature">
                <span class="mkt-feature__no">01</span>
                <h3>Frictionless capture <span>Capture · Inbox</span></h3>
                <p>
                    Save text notes, URLs, meeting notes, and documents the moment they
                    appear — no upfront classification required. Everything lands in the
                    Inbox, ready to process when you are.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="mkt-feature">
                <span class="mkt-feature__no">02</span>
                <h3>PARA organization <span>Organize · Projects, Areas, Resources, Archives</span></h3>
                <p>
                    Organize close to action with smart suggestions for project, area,
                    resource, or archive — plus tags and related notes. Flat, purposeful
                    structure instead of deep nested folders.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="mkt-feature">
                <span class="mkt-feature__no">03</span>
                <h3>Progressive summarization <span>Distill · Highlights, Summaries, Actions</span></h3>
                <p>
                    Highlight what matters, capture key takeaways, decisions, and open
                    questions, and extract action items — so a note is still useful when
                    you return to it months later.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="mkt-feature">
                <span class="mkt-feature__no">04</span>
                <h3>Projects, tasks &amp; subtasks <span>Execute · Boards, Lists, Priorities</span></h3>
                <p>
                    Every task lives in its project context with status, priority, and
                    due dates. Plan in the Tasks Hub and Calendar; execute from Today.
                    Archived work stays out of active views.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="mkt-feature">
                <span class="mkt-feature__no">05</span>
                <h3>Today screen <span>Focus · Your daily front page</span></h3>
                <p>
                    Your current task, high-priority project work, due today, overdue,
                    and what's next — one calm surface for active execution, not
                    knowledge storage.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="mkt-feature">
                <span class="mkt-feature__no">06</span>
                <h3>Goals &amp; ideas <span>Direction · Milestones, Kanban, Incubation</span></h3>
                <p>
                    Track goals with milestones and timelines, and let ideas incubate
                    until they're ready to become real projects — connected to the
                    knowledge that inspired them.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="mkt-feature">
                <span class="mkt-feature__no">07</span>
                <h3>Outputs <span>Express · Posts, Reports, Specs, Briefs</span></h3>
                <p>
                    Turn stored knowledge into blog posts, reports, product specs, and
                    meeting briefs. Brainy keeps the sources linked, so every output can
                    show its receipts.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="mkt-feature">
                <span class="mkt-feature__no">08</span>
                <h3>Trustworthy AI assistance <span>Assist · Suggestions with provenance</span></h3>
                <p>
                    AI suggests PARA placement, extracts action items, detects related
                    notes, and summarizes without losing nuance. It explains why, never
                    invents sources, and AI-generated content is always labeled — with
                    your original preserved.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="mkt-feature">
                <span class="mkt-feature__no">09</span>
                <h3>Search &amp; retrieval <span>Find · Across everything you keep</span></h3>
                <p>
                    Find notes, tasks, and outputs fast — filtered by PARA category and
                    scoped to active work by default, so archives never clutter results.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="mkt-feature">
                <span class="mkt-feature__no">10</span>
                <h3>Reversible archives <span>Preserve · Nothing is ever lost</span></h3>
                <p>
                    Archive projects, notes, and tasks with the reason preserved. Restore
                    anything at any time — inactive doesn't mean gone.
                </p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="mkt-cta">
    <div class="mkt-wrap">
        <h2 class="mkt-title">Your knowledge, ready to <em>work for you</em>.</h2>
        <p>Start free and feel the difference the first time an old note saves your day.</p>
        <div class="mkt-cta__actions">
            <a class="mkt-btn mkt-btn--onDark" href="/Account/Register">Get started free</a>
            <a class="mkt-btn mkt-btn--ghost" href="/pricing">See pricing</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
